        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A walking pad stores flat and suits walking while you do
            something else; a folding treadmill stands upright and suits real exercise.</strong>
            The pad wins on storage, weight and price; the folding treadmill wins on deck length,
            speed, incline and rails, and takes far more room even when folded.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you want the pad's storage with something to hold and the option of a light jog, a 2-in-1
            is the middle ground — our roundup of
            <a href="/best-walking-pads-with-handrail/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">walking pads with a handrail</a>
